cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Fabius: one set of rules above every model"
message: "If you cite this work, please cite the whitepaper in paper/fabius-as-a-system.pdf."
type: software
authors:
  - name: shear559
abstract: >-
  A fifteen-skill agent architecture with a router that selects relevant
  specialists, machinery and model tier over an always-on lean core.
  The decision core contains twenty-two parent routing rules developed
  in twenty-six argument blocks: twenty-two mathematical arguments under
  stated assumptions and four qualitative operational heuristics.
  A coherence analysis describes composition and precedence in that
  formalized model; it does not guarantee compliance or correctness of
  an executing agent. Evaluation retains one dated benchmark in four
  panels, including blind model-judged quality, historical execution-score
  records and model-graded factual checks, aggregate cross-family demos,
  and the hundred-task FBS suite. Gains, regressions and missing historical
  artifacts are stated explicitly. Current maintenance checks establish
  the tested behavior and release integrity, not a new benchmark gain.
version: 3.2.0
